## Private SearXNG search

{% set endpoint = vps_web.searxng_url.strip().rstrip('/') %}
{% if endpoint %}
Use the configured SearXNG endpoint for cron and sandboxed searches when
reachable from their execution environment:

- Endpoint: `{{ endpoint }}`
- JSON search: `{{ endpoint }}/search?q=<url-encoded-query>&format=json`
- The repository-managed local container needs no provider credentials and
  uses a private Valkey-backed limiter. A custom endpoint may have different
  access rules; do not assume it is public or credential-free.

Example:

```bash
curl --fail --silent --show-error --get \
  --data-urlencode 'q=Hermes Agent' \
  --data 'format=json' \
  '{{ endpoint }}/search'
```

The result contains search links and snippets. Use browser or an extractor to
read pages that require JavaScript or authentication.
{% else %}
The SearXNG endpoint is not configured (`vps_web.searxng_url` is empty).
An installed container alone does not select it as Hermes' search backend.
Use the configured web tools; do not invent an endpoint or claim sandbox/cron
search works without checking its runtime. To enable SearXNG search, propose
setting that URL in `hermes/config/vps-defaults.yml` and an authorized deploy.
{% endif %}
Do not try to pass
`BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY` or another provider secret into a cron subprocess.
